Surface: native parity port of web/src/components/ui/Accordion.tsx -- a collapsible disclosure
  (header: optional icon + title + optional badge + optional headerExtra; animated body reveal;
  controlled-or-uncontrolled open state). Mapped to the platform-idiomatic disclosure: the surface
  composes TsAccordion (a tokenized WinUI Expander), which provides the native expand/collapse
  animation, keyboard toggling, the trailing chevron (the native counterpart of the web ChevronDown
  + rotate-180) and the Narrator ExpandCollapse pattern. The web custom-button + framer-motion reveal
  is reproduced through that disclosure plus a reduce-motion-gated body fade.
  Delivered files:
    apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/Accordion.cs          (WinUI view; app-build exercised)
    apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/Accordion.Model.cs    (registration/model/projection/motion/diagnostics)
    apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/Accordion.ViewModel.cs (controlled/uncontrolled open-state holder)
    apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/AccordionTests.cs (41 headless tests)

  State coverage: the web source is purely presentational + prop-driven (its parent owns any data
  fetch), so -- like the peer presentational surfaces (InlineCallout/SwipeRow/VisuallyHidden) -- it
  has no loading/error/stale/offline chrome to reproduce. Every branch it DOES have is reproduced:
  collapsed vs expanded (body hidden/revealed, chevron 0deg/180deg), optional icon, optional badge,
  optional header-extra, controlled vs uncontrolled open, header/body padding overrides, and the
  reduced-motion (instant) vs animated body reveal.
  i18n: the surface is anonymous (the web component renders no inherent strings; title/badge/
  header-extra are caller-supplied, already-localized content), so there are NO i18n keys to add to
  the P1/S10 catalogue -- it threads the ILocalizer facade for family consistency only.

--- Pre-flight: one pre-existing integration breakage on this branch was repaired (NOT caused by Accordion) ---
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had been re-concatenated by the
  .gitattributes merge=union strategy into TWO <Project> roots (lines 1-1398 and 1399-2689) with a
  doubled, interleaved Compile item group, so it failed XML load:
    error MSB4025: The project file could not be loaded. The 'ItemGroup' start tag on line 151
    position 4 does not match the end tag of 'Project'. Line 1398, position 3.
  This made the WHOLE solution build (and every headless test) RED at baseline. Per the file's own
  INVARIANT comment, it was regenerated into a single canonical Project root -- the case-insensitive
  ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated union of every Microsoft.UI-free .cs on disk under
  dashboard-widgets/, feature-views/, misc-surfaces/, modals-dialogs/ and shared-surfaces/ (1246
  distinct) + the new Accordion Model/ViewModel links (1248 total). This is the documented,
  predecessor-sanctioned repair (see the file's INVARIANT comment and sibling logs
  0159/0166/0170/0173/0178/0185/0189). The bare WinUI view (Accordion.cs) stays excluded and is
  exercised by the app build. Verified: 1 <Project> root, 4 balanced ItemGroups, XML parses, 1248
  Compile nodes, Accordion links sorted first in the shared-surfaces block.

